Source: linux-m8x
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Antoni Aloy Torrens <aaloytorrens@gmail.com>
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), python3-dev, bc, rsync, kmod, cpio, bison, flex | flex:native, libelf-dev:native, libssl-dev:native, u-boot-tools
Homepage: https://www.kernel.org/

Package: linux-image-6.6.144-m8x-armhf
Architecture: armhf
Depends: kmod, linux-base
Provides: linux-image
Description: Linux kernel 6.6.144 (Amlogic Meson8 / m8x variant)
 This package contains the Linux kernel, modules and corresponding other
 files, version 6.6.144, specifically built for Amlogic Meson8 and Meson8m2
 TV boxes, with the meson8 changes from the xdarklight tree.
 .
 It ships a uImage for legacy Amlogic u-boot along with the device trees
 for the supported boards.

Package: linux-headers-6.6.144-m8x-armhf
Architecture: armhf
Depends: linux-image-6.6.144-m8x-armhf (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Linux kernel headers 6.6.144 (Amlogic Meson8 / m8x variant)
 This package provides kernel header files for version 6.6.144
 for building external modules against the m8x-enabled kernel.

Package: linux-libc-dev-m8x
Section: devel
Provides: linux-kernel-headers
Architecture: armhf
Multi-Arch: same
Conflicts: linux-libc-dev
Replaces: linux-libc-dev
Description: Linux support headers for userspace development (m8x variant)
 This package provides userspace headers from the Linux kernel with Amlogic
 Meson8 support. These headers are used by the installed headers for GNU
 glibc and other system libraries.

Package: linux-image-m8x
Architecture: armhf
Depends: linux-image-6.6.144-m8x-armhf (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Linux kernel (m8x) - meta package
 This is a meta-package that always depends on the latest m8x kernel.
 Installing this package will ensure you get kernel updates automatically.

Package: linux-headers-m8x
Architecture: armhf
Depends: linux-headers-6.6.144-m8x-armhf (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Linux kernel headers (m8x) - meta package
 This is a meta-package that always depends on the latest m8x kernel headers.
